[[9337,3564,"TAS had not been told that Mr Oakley suffered from Dementia and nobody had arranged for a Carer to attend with him","lack of dementia information sharing",""],[14329,5590,"There was a failure on the part of the Hospital to ensure the dissemination of Trust Policy and NPSA Guidance to all staff","lack of dissemination of Trust Policy and NPSA Guidance",""],[14330,5590,"There were weaknesses in the training systems in place","weaknesses in training systems",""],[14331,5590,"Checks were not made as to whether or not staff were up to date in their training for carrying out procedures such as the insertion of a nasogastric tube","lack of verification of staff training for procedures",""],[14332,5590,"At any one time there seemed to be a lack of knowledge as to how many trained staff were on duty to carry out such procedures","insufficient awareness of trained staff availability",""]]